{"id":"v10","level":4,"levelName":"The verb system","n":9,"of":15,"title":"The future everywhere else","titleHe":"עָתִיד בְּכָל הַבִּנְיָנִים","goal":"Read the future of pi'el, hif'il and hitpa'el — same four prefixes, different stem.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"The future you learned for pa'al was not a fact about pa'al. Every binyan builds its future the same way: א for I, נ for we, ת for you and for she, י for he and for they. What differs is the stem those letters are stuck to, and the vowel underneath them."},{"type":"table","caption":"He will — one root per binyan","head":["binyan","the tell","he will"],"rows":[["פָּעַל — write","יִ־ and a bare stem","יִכְתֹּב"],["פִּעֵל — speak","יְ־ with a shva","יְדַבֵּר"],["הִפְעִיל — explain","יַ־ with a patach","יַסְבִּיר"],["נִפְעַל — enter","יִ־ and a dagesh in the first root letter","יִכָּנֵס"],["הִתְפַּעֵל — get dressed","the ־תְ of hitpa'el survives","יִתְלַבֵּשׁ"]]},{"type":"text","body":"The prefix vowel is the fastest way to identify a verb you have never seen. יְ־ is pi'el, יַ־ is hif'il, and the הִת of hitpa'el is unmistakable in any tense."},{"type":"binyan","he":"פִּעֵל","en":"pi'el","note":"Often an intensified or causative sense; the middle root letter doubles.","verb":{"root":"ד־ב־ר","inf":"לְדַבֵּר","en":"to speak"},"tense":"future","rows":[{"label":"I","he":"אֲנִי","form":"אֲדַבֵּר"},{"label":"you (m.)","he":"אַתָּה","form":"תְּדַבֵּר"},{"label":"you (f.)","he":"אַתְּ","form":"תְּדַבְּרִי"},{"label":"he","he":"הוּא","form":"יְדַבֵּר"},{"label":"she","he":"הִיא","form":"תְּדַבֵּר"},{"label":"we","he":"אֲנַחְנוּ","form":"נְדַבֵּר"},{"label":"you (m.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּם","form":"תְּדַבְּרוּ"},{"label":"you (f.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּן","form":"תְּדַבְּרוּ"},{"label":"they","he":"הֵם / הֵן","form":"יְדַבְּרוּ"}]},{"type":"binyan","he":"הִפְעִיל","en":"hif'il","note":"Causative — making someone else do or become something.","verb":{"root":"ס־ב־ר","inf":"לְהַסְבִּיר","en":"to explain"},"tense":"future","rows":[{"label":"I","he":"אֲנִי","form":"אַסְבִּיר"},{"label":"you (m.)","he":"אַתָּה","form":"תַּסְבִּיר"},{"label":"you (f.)","he":"אַתְּ","form":"תַּסְבִּירִי"},{"label":"he","he":"הוּא","form":"יַסְבִּיר"},{"label":"she","he":"הִיא","form":"תַּסְבִּיר"},{"label":"we","he":"אֲנַחְנוּ","form":"נַסְבִּיר"},{"label":"you (m.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּם","form":"תַּסְבִּירוּ"},{"label":"you (f.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּן","form":"תַּסְבִּירוּ"},{"label":"they","he":"הֵם / הֵן","form":"יַסְבִּירוּ"}]},{"type":"binyan","he":"הִתְפַּעֵל","en":"hitpa'el","note":"Reflexive — the action comes back on the one doing it.","verb":{"root":"ל־ב־ש","inf":"לְהִתְלַבֵּשׁ","en":"to get dressed"},"tense":"future","rows":[{"label":"I","he":"אֲנִי","form":"אֶתְלַבֵּשׁ"},{"label":"you (m.)","he":"אַתָּה","form":"תִּתְלַבֵּשׁ"},{"label":"you (f.)","he":"אַתְּ","form":"תִּתְלַבְּשִׁי"},{"label":"he","he":"הוּא","form":"יִתְלַבֵּשׁ"},{"label":"she","he":"הִיא","form":"תִּתְלַבֵּשׁ"},{"label":"we","he":"אֲנַחְנוּ","form":"נִתְלַבֵּשׁ"},{"label":"you (m.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּם","form":"תִּתְלַבְּשׁוּ"},{"label":"you (f.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּן","form":"תִּתְלַבְּשׁוּ"},{"label":"they","he":"הֵם / הֵן","form":"יִתְלַבְּשׁוּ"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"Two cells always collide: תְּ־ is both you (m. sing.) and she. הִיא תְּדַבֵּר and אַתָּה תְּדַבֵּר are the same word, and only the pronoun or the context tells them apart. Hebrew has lived with this for three thousand years; you will too."},{"type":"tip","body":"In speech the plural feminine forms have gone. Nobody says תְּדַבֵּרְנָה — they say תְּדַבְּרוּ for everyone. You will still meet the old forms in print, which is why the tables carry them."}],"vocab":[{"he":"יְדַבֵּר","en":"he will speak","translit":"yedaber"},{"he":"יַסְבִּיר","en":"he will explain","translit":"yasbir"},{"he":"יִכָּנֵס","en":"he will go in","translit":"yikanes"},{"he":"יִתְלַבֵּשׁ","en":"he will get dressed","translit":"yitlabesh"},{"he":"נְדַבֵּר","en":"we will speak","translit":"nedaber"},{"he":"אַסְבִּיר","en":"I will explain","translit":"asbir"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["he will speak","lesson","tries","gets up"],"correct":0,"prompt":"יְדַבֵּר","translit":"yedaber"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["only, yet","he will explain","a comma","price"],"correct":1,"prompt":"יַסְבִּיר","translit":"yasbir"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["forty","he will go in","the penitential prayers","Shvat (Jan–Feb)"],"correct":1,"prompt":"יִכָּנֵס","translit":"yikanes"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["cloud","he will get dressed","waits","hands"],"correct":1,"prompt":"יִתְלַבֵּשׁ","translit":"yitlabesh"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["we will speak","childhood","third","slow"],"correct":0,"prompt":"נְדַבֵּר","translit":"nedaber"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["I will explain","strength, power","the blessing over wine","prophet"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אַסְבִּיר","translit":"asbir"},{"type":"choice","q":"get dressed — we, future","options":["תִּתְלַבֵּשׁ","תִּתְלַבְּשִׁי","אֶתְלַבֵּשׁ","נִתְלַבֵּשׁ"],"correct":3,"he":true,"why":"הִתְפַּעֵל, future: we is נִתְלַבֵּשׁ."},{"type":"choice","q":"get dressed — you (f.pl.), future","options":["תִּתְלַבְּשׁוּ","תִּתְלַבְּשִׁי","תִּתְלַבֵּשׁ","אֶתְלַבֵּשׁ"],"correct":0,"he":true,"why":"הִתְפַּעֵל, future: you (f.pl.) is תִּתְלַבְּשׁוּ."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “he will speak”?","options":["מִנְיָן","אָנֹכִי","יְדַבֵּר","פּוּרִים"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"get dressed — they, future","options":["תִּתְלַבֵּשׁ","יִתְלַבְּשׁוּ","אֶתְלַבֵּשׁ","תִּתְלַבְּשִׁי"],"correct":1,"he":true,"why":"הִתְפַּעֵל, future: they is יִתְלַבְּשׁוּ."},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["נְדַבֵּר","אַסְבִּיר","יִכָּנֵס","יַסְבִּיר"],"correct":3,"say":"יַסְבִּיר","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"explain — he, future","options":["אַסְבִּיר","תַּסְבִּירִ